# Which of the three reasons each question has taken. One row per question that takes a typed
# blank: its reasons as a three-letter word, and how many filings stand behind it.
#
# The split is a schema boundary
#   The rows are sorted so that the questions reaching `none` sit together, and the ones that never
#   do sit together. The split is not cosmetic: it is the `pm:Absence` / `pm:ClaimAbsence`
#   boundary, printed from the data rather than read off the schema, and a question on the wrong
#   side of it is a defect.
#
# Sorted on the letter, not the string
#   A collation that files punctuation after letters buries the split this query exists to show,
#   so the `none` letter is pulled out and ordered explicitly.
-- §12  Every question that takes a typed blank, as a three-letter word: n·u·a.
SELECT m.question       AS "question!",
       m.mask           AS "mask!",
       m.filings        AS "filings!",
       m.as_none        AS "as_none!"
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/state_masks.sqlc)
) m
ORDER BY (m.mask LIKE 'n%') DESC, m.filings DESC, m.question
